 to work together  now sylvie says they just need enough  power to recharge the tim pad so they  can travel through interdimensional time  and space  this is because the tva essentially  exists outside of time  and the tim pads allow the tba members  to travel from outside of time  into different timelines and time  periods now as they walk to find power  this is where we find out that sylvie  was indeed loki  she says that's not who i am anymore i'm  sylvie now  it's an alias now from here we  essentially learn what sylvie's plan was  and loki is the one that actually tells  us he says your plan was to tear the  place down  create the ultimate power vacuum of  destruction and walk away  and silvi basically says yep this would  ultimately accomplish her  purpose of tearing down the tva and  getting rid of the timekeepers and  essentially creating a multiverse of  madness a multiverse where she has true  freedom and her fate isn't decided by  the timekeepers but she might also have  a different motive here  later on in the episode she states that  she had been running from the tva since  she was very very young so perhaps this  simply could just be about her  trying to get the tva off her back and  the only way to do that  is to destroy them now loki and sylvia  come across somebody who is actually in  their home  loki says brute force won't work so  silvia opens the door to immediately get  shot by some kind of energy cannon or  some type of sound wave cannon  loki attempts to try and trick the lady  by transforming into her old husband but  she sees right through him ultimately  the lady tells them that there's an ark  that takes off it's going to leave the  moon and save whoever is on it and the  way to get there  is by train however to get on the train  you need a ticket we get there and we  hear some people say they're only giving  out tickets to the wealthy and here we  start to see more differences between  loki and sylvie even though they are the  same  just 