 may not be a princess  so perhaps whatever happened in her  timeline resulted in her not being  a princess of asgard and then we get the  really big reveal  that loki is actually bisexual sylvie  asked him if he ever had any princesses  or  princes waiting for him and he says a  bit of both  and if there is any confusion on whether  or not this means he's bisexual the  director  kate herron did come out on twitter and  state that it was very important to her  and one of her goals to acknowledge that  loki was bisexual so if you are somewhat  confused  don't be loki is bisexual this is canon  to the mcu confirmed and it's a pretty  big deal and i'm happy for those people  who this means a lot to  now sylvia actually ends up falling  asleep and she wakes up to a drunken  loki singing in between english and  asgardian now here when he finishes his  drink he slams it on the ground and  yells another this is just like what  thor did in the very first thor film  when he's drinking coffee in the diner  he drinks his coffee throws a glass on  the ground and yells another  [Music]  now during all the chaos we actually  learned something about sylvie she  says she's paranoid because she spent  her entire life  running from the omniscient fascist you  work for now of course she is referring  to the tva who she calls the time police  now this may have significant meaning  this may mean that  sylvie or this loki variant is different  from the others  did she commit a crime that made the tva  chase her or perhaps were they trying to  get her for something else  clearly the time keepers aren't exactly  the best of people as they are taking  variants and  essentially erasing their memories and  then brainwashing them since the tva can  see into the future  maybe they realize that sylvie is  actually their doom  and that's the reason they've been  chasing her her entire life i'm sure  there's more to this that will be  revealed in future episodes  now loki is drunk and it doesn't really  work out for the two of them  the guards come and because loki is  drunk when he tries to use his magic to  create fake tickets he ends up doing  fireworks again that he showed sylvia  before  this of course leads to a fight and  there are two key moments here  one of them is we see more magic being  used by loki he actually uses his magic  in the form of green energy blast  something we've never seen before the  second part is silvie actually takes off  her horns or i should say horn  and uses it to stab one of the guards  and then if you notice  one of the guards actually ends up  throwing it back at her but she dodges  it  however she never picks it back up loki  gets thrown out of the window and since  he has the tin pad she jumps after him  and if you notice from here on out she  never wears it again because it's still  on the train  now when they both finally land on the  ground and get up sylvie puts her sword  to loki's throat and says give me the  temp pad  and loki says okay and he reveals that  it's broken  however i don't believe this to be true  i believe this is an  illusion by loki every time sylvie has  asked for the tin pad loki has said  no he's refused to give it to her this  entire time and of course knowing loki's  character he would never give it to her  however in this scene  he immediately says okay so i don't  believe this is the real temp pad i  believe he's still holding on to it and  i think this will be revealed next  episode and i think this is going to be  how they get off of lomantus one because  at the end of the episode the ark got  destroyed which was seemingly their only  way out  however more on that in just a bit now  from here we actually see a little bit  more of  sylvie's powers silvi states that loki  pretty much destroyed her mission and  loki kind of taunts her stating that you  can't beat them referring to the tva and  the timekeepers  from here her hands light up green and  she emits an explosive blast of  essentially anger and these blasts are  kind of similar to the one that loki did  on the train  now from here loki proposes that they go  and take over the ark and essentially  make sure it gets  off of the moon sylvia agrees and the  two of them start to walk towards the  ark and here is where we get  two big reveals one is that sylvie and  loki kind of start to trust each other  and sylvie reveals how her enchantment  works she reveals that she has to make  physical contact which is why we see her  fingers  actually touch the heads of who she  enchants then she has to grab their  minds and she explains that the weak  minds are pretty easy to take over the  stronger ones however require a bit  of work and she has to create fantasies  from their memories  to stay in control and this is where the  second big reveal comes  she says that the young soldier from the  tva's mind was messed  up it was very clouded and she had to  pull memories from hundreds of years ago  before she even fought for the tva  and this is huge news loki says i  thought the tva were created by the  timekeepers in which sylvie says that's  ridiculous they're all  variants and of course this is news to  us and loki and loki states that they  don't know that even the variants that  work for the tva don't know that but  that is because as sylvia explained  their mind is being clouded most likely  by the time keepers  or king now from here sylvie and loki  make it to the ark but right as they get  there  the planet that the moon is about to  crash into breaks in half and debris  from it starts to crash into the ground  from here sylvie and loki run around  randomly fighting guards  trying to find their way onto the ark  and here's where we see a very  very interesting scene a pillar is  falling down  and loki says i got it and then stops  the pillar from falling  however if you take a close look at this  he's not just using telekinesis to stop  it from falling it looks like he is  actually reversing  its time if you pay careful attention it  seems very clear that he  reversed it so does loki have the  ability to make  objects go backwards in time i'm not so  sure about that  however we do know that loki did come in  contact  with a lot of infinity stones inside of  the tva  and of course it's loki he most likely  took some so  does he have the time stone on him and  could he have perhaps  used that time stone to stop this pillar  in time and then  reverse it now we didn't see the time  stone or anything glow green or any  runes pop up like they do for doctor  strange but this  is loki he knows magic so perhaps he  could have manipulated the time stone in  some way  and reverse this pillar from falling  because remember the time stone and the  infinity stones don't work inside of the  tva  but in this scene they're not in the tva  they're outside of the tva on  a timeline lomantis one so the time  stone  would work here loki is the god of  mischief so i do think ultimately he  took a handful of infinity stones for  himself because of course he was  planning his escape the entire time and  when he finally escaped in his mind he  would have a bunch of infinity stones to  use but you'll have to let me know what  you think about this  do you think it's the time stone or do  you think loki actually has this ability  somehow  now overall i know a lot of people in my  live chat last night said that this  episode was pretty underwhelming but  after watching it again  i think it might have been my favorite  episode i love the dynamic between  sylvie and loki there were a lot of  amazing scenes in it that were very  cinematic there were also some very  quiet tinder scenes that i enjoyed there  were some big reveals about loki's  powers and then of course we had the big  tva reveal which also revealed that  there is a  big villain behind the tva but let me  know in the comments down below  what you would rate this episode 1 out  of 10. 10 being the highest  don't forget to like 